# Performance, feedback and quality learning — Vajra Global

Version: 0.6 (historical style source and pilot claim handling clarified)
Last updated: 2026-11-18    
Human review: Approved for internal pilot use per explicit user instruction on 2026-11-10; approver name/role not supplied. This does not independently verify source facts, grant public reuse permissions, or remove item-level provisional, disputed, expired, or evidence requirements.
Owner: Analyst / editor (roles in architecture; named owner not supplied)  
Review cycle: monthly and after each content cycle

> Sources: onboarding pack PDF, pp. 38–49 and 56–62, and the supplied LinkedIn workbook. Historical KPI values are transcribed as reported; the post-level records and feedback reflect the workbook fields.

## K4.1 Historical KPI figures (Apr–Sep 2025)

The source defines this as LinkedIn performance except organic social traffic, which is cross-platform. These historical values are not current targets.

| Metric | Apr 2025 | May | Jun | Jul | Aug | Sep | Source caveat |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| Organic clicks | 1,156 | 341 | 561 | 284 | 3,197 | 960 | Aug 2025 clicks flagged for verification in final map |
| Organic impressions | 10,960 | 5,872 | 4,889 | 6,281 | 9,000 | 4,200 | As transcribed from workbook |
| LinkedIn page followers | 1,695 | 1,792 | 1,930 | 1,996 | 2,019 | 2,128 | As transcribed from workbook |
| LinkedIn posts published | 7 | 8 | 6 | 8 | 9 | 8 | As transcribed from workbook |
| LinkedIn page engagement rate — historical measure | 15.62% | 12.92% | 13.84% | 6.98% | 7.24% | 15.45% | Formula not established as equivalent to other series |
| Organic social traffic — historical measure | 13.15% | 14.03% | 17.62% | 7.97% | 10.99% | 13.19% | Cross-platform; denominator and attribution method undocumented |

The workbook also contains an October–December historical engagement series recorded as October 15.9, November 33.7, December 27.0; the source says definitions/reporting periods are not established as equivalent. Preserve separately; confirm units and years before use (p. 39).

The April–September 2025 table remains a transcription of historical reported values from the PDF; it is not the baseline for the November 2026 pilot. The pilot target is approximately 5,700 LinkedIn organic impressions across six posts, as directed by the user. The target is separate from the current baseline data described below. Do not treat the 2025 monthly values as measurements taken in November 2026, infer causality, or treat other metrics as pilot KPIs. Keep cross-platform organic traffic separate and retain the two engagement-rate series separately until their formulas are verified.

## K4.2 Post-level data schema

For each published post, capture: post ID/URL/date; content owner; pillar/topic/campaign; format; final caption; creative reference; impressions, clicks (with definition), reactions, comments, reposts, engagements and engagement rate; page visits/follower growth/enquiries where available; source; extraction date; and completeness status. The current baseline for this pilot is the supplied LinkedIn dataset below: 63 post-level records with Published dates spanning April–October 2026. All 63 records include impressions; together they total 30,823 impressions, with a mean of 489.3 and median of 381 impressions per record. These are descriptive summaries of the supplied baseline data, not the pilot target. Use the supplied Published dates for time-based comparisons. The earlier PDF did not include a complete, consistently structured three-month post-level export; the newer workbook now provides post-level data for performance review.

**Post-level records — LinkedIn workbook, April 2026 to October 2026**

Records are listed in workbook order. Published date values are copied from the supplied Published date field. The 63 records have Published dates spanning April–October 2026. No dates are calculated. Blank workbook values are omitted; fields with no column in the workbook are marked Not provided.

