.NET 8 reaches end of support on 10 November 2026, followed by Umbraco 13 on 14 December 2026.

Your website will continue to function after these dates. But running on unsupported technology brings security risks, compatibility concerns and some difficult decisions for your IT team.

🔍 So, should you upgrade your existing website to Umbraco 17 or consider a fresh build?

That decision deserves more thought than simply comparing development costs.

Umbraco 17 brings significant architectural changes, including a new back-office extension model, changes to the Rich Text Editor, and updated caching capabilities. For websites with custom functionality and third-party integrations, these changes can have implications for migration.

And there is another consideration. What happens if your business cannot complete the migration before December?

💡 Our latest blog examines the technical challenges, migration options, testing requirements and the role of Extended Long-Term Support (XLTS).

At Vajra Global, we help businesses assess their existing Umbraco implementations and plan migrations based on their technical requirements.

📖 𝐏𝐥𝐚𝐧𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐲𝐨𝐮𝐫 𝐧𝐞𝐱𝐭 𝐦𝐨𝐯𝐞? 𝐑𝐞𝐚𝐝 𝐨𝐮𝐫 𝐠𝐮𝐢𝐝𝐞 𝐛𝐞𝐟𝐨𝐫𝐞 𝐝𝐞𝐜𝐢𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐨𝐧 𝐲𝐨𝐮𝐫 𝐦𝐢𝐠𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝐚𝐩𝐩𝐫𝐨𝐚𝐜𝐡.

🔗 https://lnkd.in/gGCHqZhX

#Umbraco17 #UmbracoMigration #CMSMigration #WebsiteModernisation
```

