```text
Enterprise leaders are under pressure to move faster, yet website projects often remain one of the slowest initiatives to execute.

The process has traditionally depended on multiple teams working one after another, creating delays that compound over time.

AI is changing that equation.⚡

Not because websites can now be built with a few prompts. Any business can do that.

The bigger change is happening inside the development process itself.

Research, UX, content structuring, design exploration, coding, testing, SEO preparation, and quality checks can now happen simultaneously rather than waiting for one stage to finish before the next begins.

That changes what enterprises should expect from their agency.

⏱️ Faster delivery without cutting corners
🔍 Better-informed decisions before development starts
📈 Stronger use of budgets and specialist expertise
🤖 AI agents working alongside human experts, not replacing them

The agencies that adapt their operating model will look very different from those that simply add AI tools to an existing workflow.

So what should enterprise leaders be asking their agency in 2026?

Our latest article explores how AI-first web development is changing expectations around speed, cost, quality, and the way digital experiences are delivered.

