Caption:

```text
Most content teams are still measuring visibility the old way. 📊

Rankings. Traffic. Click-through rates.

But AI assistants have introduced another layer of discovery: citations inside AI-generated responses.

And the rules behind citations are different from the rules behind ranking.

In our latest article, Karpagavalli Krishnasamy and Swetha Sitaraman unpack what happens between “being retrieved” and “being cited” inside platforms like ChatGPT, drawing on recent Ahrefs and Semrush research, along with observations from enterprise content programmes we’ve worked on.

A few takeaways:
• Ranking on page one does not guarantee AI visibility
• Intent-aligned titles influence whether AI systems even open your page
• Human-refined content still outperforms purely AI-generated output in critical positions
• Structured knowledge ecosystems matter far more than high-volume publishing

The teams gaining visibility today are thinking carefully about content structure, topical depth, FAQs, schema markup, and answer-ready formatting.

The article also explores the growing gap between AI-generated content and AI-optimised content strategy - a distinction many organisations are still missing.

👉 Read the full piece here:
[https://lnkd.in/gc5DdSwu](https://lnkd.in/gc5DdSwu)

🧠 Worth reading for anyone working across SEO, content, MarOps, or demand generation.

#AISearch #AEO #SEO #ContentMarketing #MarTech #B2BContent #GenerativeAI #MarketingOperations
```

