Caption:

```text
🚀 HubSpot is rebuilding its Salesforce integration with a new “v2” sync engine.;

The upgrade marks a major backend refactoring designed to deliver faster, more resilient, and more flexible Salesforce data synchronisation for customers.

👉 Key enhancements on the v2 platform include:
• Enhanced de-duplication using any field
• Owner field synchronisation
• Support for unique IDs beyond email addresses
• Fewer sync errors with faster resolution
• Inclusion lists for any synced object

HubSpot has already migrated custom objects, tickets, and activities to the v2 engine. Support for company objects is now live, introducing one of the platform’s most requested capabilities - the ability to merge company records in HubSpot while automatically remapping them to Salesforce.

📌 Deal object support is expected in the coming weeks, while work on contact objects will continue through Q2, with a beta planned later this year. HubSpot aims to fully deprecate the legacy sync engine by mid-2027.

💡 This move highlights a broader change taking place across the MarTech ecosystem: businesses now expect integrations to handle larger data volumes, complex workflows, and cleaner synchronisation with fewer operational bottlenecks.

🤝 Looking to optimise your HubSpot–Salesforce integration? Connect with us to explore how we can help your business improve data synchronisation, reduce operational friction, and build a more connected revenue ecosystem.

Ganapathy Sankarabaaham Sriram Purushothaman Aravindh Purushothaman Sabapathy TK Rea Kurian Shashidhar Bellur Adarsh Noronha

#HubSpot #Salesforce #MarTech #CRM #MarketingTechnology #RevOps #DigitalTransformation #HubSpotPlatinumPartner
```

