### K5.2 Provisional editorial standards

The PDF labels these **provisional** until actual reviewer history is consolidated. `[P]`: strong relevant hook; business relevance; clear Vajra point of view; verifiable statistics/technical statements/references; brand alignment; accessible clarity; relevant CTA; non-generic promotional tone; readable uncluttered creative; no unapproved client, employee or internal information. Do not turn these into approved formal rules without sign-off.

## K8 Benchmarks and rubric

### Candidate strong examples — provisional, unrated

The PDF names three Oct 2026 candidates, not formally rated best-performing posts: ChatGPT Ads thought-leadership article (Oct 8); AI and Creative Judgement article (Oct 14); Umbraco 13-to-17 migration article (Oct 26). The source says formal reviewer scoring is still required. Do not assert these are top-performing posts.

### Weak examples

W1 generic AI post, W2 service-heavy promotional post, W3 technical jargon post are synthetic examples. The source's weak examples and rewrites are training material, not actual Vajra posts. Keep that distinction in any use.

### K8.3 Quality rubric (source, p. 58)

Score 1–5 for brand voice, clarity, accuracy and CTA. The source defines 1 as poor, 3 acceptable and 5 excellent for those dimensions. Additional review dimensions: strategic relevance, audience relevance, originality/distinctiveness, visual quality and evidence quality. The exact scoring anchors for additional dimensions are not provided here.

## Open items

- Verify the flagged August 2025 clicks before relying on that historical value.
- Confirm organic-social traffic denominator/attribution and historical engagement series units/formulas.
- Do not set forward targets from this baseline without current baseline and business approval.
- Gather real reviewer history; formally score candidate benchmark posts; keep synthetic weak posts labeled.
- Evaluation store is separate from runtime knowledge. Do not place K9/K10 answer keys or seeded faulty posts in this file.
